          <!-- PROJECT 1: TaskFlow -->
          <article class="card project-card">
            <div class="project-thumb">
              <img src="icon-512.png" alt="TaskFlow app screenshot" loading="lazy" />
              <span class="project-badge">Web App</span>
            </div>
            <div class="project-body">
              <h3>TaskFlow</h3>
              <p>An offline-first task manager with due dates, priorities, and a native-app feel. No sign-up required.</p>

              <details class="project-details">
  <summary>Read case study</summary>
  <div class="details-content">
    <p><strong>The Problem:</strong> Most to-do apps force you to create an account and stay online just to check off a task. For people with older phones or unreliable data, simple productivity is frustrating.</p>
    <p><strong>The Solution:</strong> TaskFlow opens instantly and works completely offline. It features due dates, priorities, dark mode, and can be installed like a native app — no sign-ups, no loading screens.</p>
    <p><strong>The Tech:</strong> Built with plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Uses the Service Worker API for offline caching. No databases, no frameworks.</p>
  </div>
</details>
              <div class="tech-tags">
                <span>HTML</span><span>CSS</span><span>JavaScript</span><span>PWA</span>
              </div>
              <div class="project-links">
                <a href="https://mustaphyambal-maker.github.io/taskflow/" class="link-live" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Live Demo</a>
                <a href="https://github.com/mustaphyambal-maker/taskflow" class="link-code" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Code</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

